# Rank 1127 / CVE-2025-68121: Go's crypto/tls resumed a TLS session using a
# certificate chain cached from the original handshake, checking only that
# the cached chain had not expired and never re-checking that its root was
# still trusted under the current Config, so a Config mutated between the
# original and resumed handshakes (Config.Clone() plus mutation, or
# GetConfigForClient returning a different Config) could let a resumed
# session succeed with a chain that would be rejected on a fresh handshake
# (CWE-295).
#
# anyUnexpiredChain in src/crypto/tls/common.go walked verifiedChains, the
# chains verified during the original handshake and cached in the session
# state, and returned true if any chain had no expired certificate, with no
# reference to the Config in play for the resumption at all.
#
# Pool commit 026fa9dc597e is the real fix (COMMIT_OK; the nocommit flag on
# this rank is a false positive from the repository-linking heuristic, since
# the advisory's structured repository field names the advisory database
# itself rather than golang/go; the commit's own message states "Updates
# CVE-2025-68121" and matches Go issue #77217 and Gerrit CL 737700 exactly).
# It renames the function to anyValidVerifiedChain, adds an x509.VerifyOptions
# built from the CURRENT Config's RootCAs/ClientCAs, and after the expiry
# check calls root.Verify(opts) on each chain's root certificate against that
# live trust store before accepting the resumption. No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, and the same dependency-only shape recorded repeatedly this
# batch (ranks 1083, 1097, 1101, 1103, 1105, 1112, 1122), here inside the Go
# standard library itself rather than a third-party package: any application
# calling crypto/tls the ordinary way looks identical before and after this
# fix, since the entire defect is internal to how the standard library
# revalidates a cached certificate chain, and the only remedy is upgrading
# the Go toolchain. Scanning either revision of common.go reports the same
# one unrelated lock-lifecycle finding. code.CertValidationDisabled
# (VYQL-CFG-004) carries the same CWE_295 exactly and is the nearest concept
# in the ontology, but its bindings look for certificate validation being
# turned off outright (InsecureSkipVerify and its equivalents across
# languages), a single explicit flag; this bug has no such flag anywhere,
# validation stays nominally on throughout, and what silently narrows is
# which trust store a cached result is checked against between two
# handshakes, a relationship between two points in time that a presence
# pattern over one flag cannot express.
#
# No definition change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1127: resumption accepts a cached chain checked only for expiry"
  lang go
  file common.go
  reject VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  package tls

  import (
      "crypto/x509"
      "slices"
      "time"
  )

  func anyUnexpiredChain(verifiedChains [][]*x509.Certificate, now time.Time) bool {
      for _, chain := range verifiedChains {
          if len(chain) != 0 && !slices.ContainsFunc(chain, func(cert *x509.Certificate) bool {
              return now.Before(cert.NotBefore) || now.After(cert.NotAfter)
          }) {
              return true
          }
      }
      return false
  }
  ```

test "rank1127: resumption also revalidates the cached chain's root against the current Config"
  lang go
  file common.go
  reject VYQL-CFG-004
  code
  ```
  package tls

  import (
      "crypto/x509"
      "slices"
  )

  func anyValidVerifiedChain(verifiedChains [][]*x509.Certificate, opts x509.VerifyOptions) bool {
      for _, chain := range verifiedChains {
          if len(chain) == 0 {
              continue
          }
          if slices.ContainsFunc(chain, func(cert *x509.Certificate) bool {
              return opts.CurrentTime.Before(cert.NotBefore) || opts.CurrentTime.After(cert.NotAfter)
          }) {
              continue
          }
          root := chain[len(chain)-1]
          if _, err := root.Verify(opts); err == nil {
              return true
          }
      }
      return false
  }
  ```
